      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then the integral equals \\( \\left[\\frac{x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} - \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} \\, dx \\), and the boundary term is \\( \\frac{\\pi}{8} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            "Pi",
            8
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The remaining integral is \\( \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} \\, dx = \\frac{1}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So the value is \\( \\frac{\\pi}{8} - \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) = - \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{\\pi}{8} \\).",
